== file {"schemaId": "opensip.relation.file.v1", "selector": "#/$defs/FilePayloadV1", "universeRule": "same-only", "subjectKind": "source-path", "anchorLaw": {"class": "inventory", "cardinality": 0, "rule": "The claim is the snapshot inventory row itself: path, content digest and byte length, all joined by this relation`s own inventoried-file snapshotJoin over the retained bytes. Nothing further was read, so nothing further is cited."}, "ladder": ["enumerated"], "coverageTotality": {"rung": "enumerated", "over": "subjects", "matchOn": ["snapshotId", "relation", "resolution", "sourceUniverse", "targetUniverse"], "matchLaw": "A fact discharges THIS scope's obligation only if it agrees with the scope on EVERY coordinate listed in matchOn. Those are the four CoverageKeyV2 coordinates other than the subject-scope commitment itself, plus the owning snapshot. An earlier revision matched relation and resolution ALONE, and that is not enough in a view that carries more than one universe: the view-level fact/scope join is EXISTENTIAL - each fact must agree with SOME scope on relation, rung and both universes - so a TypeScript file fact is lawfully in a view that also carries a syntax-universe scope, and it then paid that scope's missing-file obligation. A complete Run exhibited exactly that (root diagnostic attempt3: two complete file@enumerated scopes for `a.ts`, only the TypeScript fact, ADMIT). Totality is a claim about what THIS universe examined, so it must be discharged by evidence produced in THIS universe; a fact from another universe is a different interpretation of the same bytes and is not the same observation.", "snapshotIsListedDeliberately": "The owning snapshot is already forced transitively - Run closure requires every fact and every subject-scope to carry the Run's own snapshotId - so listing it changes no outcome today, and a control confirms the transitive refusal (REFERENCE_SOURCE_JOIN). It is listed anyway because this law reads ONE scope's obligation out of a SHARED view, and a join that silently depends on an invariant enforced somewhere else is the same class of implicit coupling that produced the cross-universe defect.", "pathField": "path", "rule": "When a subject-scope for file@enumerated carries entry.coverage `complete`, every one of its subjects that appears in the analysed snapshot sourceInventory must have an admitted file@enumerated fact in the same view whose payload `path` is that subject. A subject outside the inventory is owed nothing.", "refusal": "COVERAGE_INVENTORY_TOTALITY_OMITS_PATH"}, "rungs": {}}
== imports {"schemaId": "opensip.relation.imports.v1", "selector": "#/$defs/ImportsPayloadV1", "universeRule": "admitted-target", "subjectKind": "symbol", "anchorLaw": {"class": "source-text", "minimum": 1, "rule": "Every span this fact was read from; at least one, because an unanchored code fact names no file that could have been read."}, "ladder": ["syntactic-specifier", "resolved-target"], "rungs": {"syntactic-specifier": {"required": [], "forbidden": ["resolvedTarget"]}, "resolved-target": {"required": ["resolvedTarget"], "forbidden": []}}}
== literal {"schemaId": "opensip.relation.literal.v1", "selector": "#/$defs/LiteralPayloadV1", "universeRule": "same-only", "subjectKind": "symbol", "anchorLaw": {"class": "source-text", "minimum": 1, "rule": "Every span this fact was read from; at least one, because an unanchored code fact names no file that could have been read."}, "ladder": ["syntactic"], "rungs": {}}
