===== CapabilityAvailabilityV1
{
 "type": "object",
 "additionalProperties": false,
 "required": [
  "stepCount",
  "totalNoticeCount",
  "steps"
 ],
 "properties": {
  "stepCount": {
   "$ref": "#/$defs/Uint53"
  },
  "totalNoticeCount": {
   "$ref": "#/$defs/Uint53"
  },
  "steps": {
   "type": "array",
   "minItems": 0,
   "maxItems": 64,
   "uniqueItems": true,
   "items": {
    "$ref": "#/$defs/CapabilityAvailabilityStepV1"
   },
   "x-opensip-order": "sequence"
  }
 },
 "description": "The invocation's availability account, composed PER STEP. An earlier revision used one flat array bounded at 1024 and argued it could not truncate because that is the analysis-spec bound - but 1024 is per analysis-spec, not per invocation, and a named multi-step invocation carries up to 64 steps: two admitted selections of 1023 requests each compose 2046 notices and the flat array refused. Composing per step preserves every valid admitted invocation: each step keeps its own bounded collection, `steps` is bounded by the invocation step bound (StepId 0..63), and no notice is ever discarded to fit. `totalNoticeCount` is the sum of the step counts and is authoritative for a caller counting absences across the invocation. A step that made no selection - a skipped step, or a non-analysis step - contributes NO entry; a step that selected and found nothing absent contributes an entry with an empty array, which is the positive statement that it checked. A retried step keeps ONE entry, for the attempt whose selection the invocation retained."
}
